name: Ground Floor
# The first floor of the game, made by hand: learn the moves, get the power
# on, take the lift up. North: the two-storey lobby (west: entrance,
# reception, lifts), the open plan, two offices. A corridor the width of the
# floor. South: the secretary's office and the boss's through it, the
# lounge, the meeting room, the plant room (servers; the breaker in the
# switch room behind). The route: blue pass (reception) -> open plan ->
# corridor -> red pass (the boss's desk) -> plant room -> breaker -> lifts.
# [floor] values on wall cells make low blocks, in eighths of a wall:
# 2 = desk (0.68 m), 3 = counter (1 m). Wall types: a = table, b = executive desk,
# c = single steel desk,
# d = two 1980s steel desks back to back, j = the same with cubicle screens,
# k = lift car walls (steel inside, the area's look outside)
# on top. [facing] says which way a desk's
# front (where you sit) faces; for stairs (h) the way they go up. f = curtain
# wall, g = entrance doors, i = balcony (railed); [ceiling] g = 16/8, a
# double-height space. [areas]: l lobby, e executive, s service, c lift car, . office
# (floors, ceilings, and how plain # walls look from each side). See docs/GAME.md.

